}

sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Benthic stickleback cellular Turing wavelength (43 µm, Holocene 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Gasterosteus aculeatus_benthic morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gasterosteus aculeatus_benthic specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/gasterosteus_aculeatus_benthic_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Gasterosteus aculeatus_benthic; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Low-plate Eda alleles and Pitx1 pelvic-enhancer deletion distinguish post-glacial benthic sticklebacks from the complete-plate marine ancestor (Colosimo 2005; Chan 2010). | Juvenile pigment patterns in threespine sticklebacks are genetically divergent (Greenwood et al. 2011); Kit ligand dosage changes pigmentation (Miller et al. 2007). | Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979 define k_c. Kondo and Asai 1995 and Nakamasu et al. 2009 show activator-inhibitor chromatophore patterns in other teleosts.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg integration with a=0.1, b=0.9, gamma=0.3, Du=0.55, Dv=12, seed 3234, and dx chosen so linear λ_c = 43.15 µm. | Twelve PDE snapshots rendered with the steady two-morphogen readout; last frame held to the azimuthal fit. | Du sweep at fixed dx, equal-diffusion ablation, four full-length seeds, plate foreground mask, activator-only correlation.; transfer_boundary: Zebrafish and angelfish rate constants are not benthic-stickleback measurements. | 43 µm is the catalog detail-tier assignment, not a published melanophore count on G. aculeatus.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Commons lateral photograph (Ron Offermans, CC BY-SA 3.0) is a benthic low-plate fish. | Does not claim the gallery detail plate is a raw 43 µm lattice micrograph. | Does not claim the 2.2 mm organ-scale benthic model. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication. No local nanopub profile was present.]; phenomenon_size: 32 µm (3.168e-05 m, log10=-4.499 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 32 µm to 9.9 cm): 32 µm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-bioelectric-polarity, 118 µm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-vertex-packing, 2.2 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-turing-wavelength, 4.1 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-clock-wavefront, 9.6 mm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-elastic-buckling, 1.3 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-morphogen-condensation, 1.7 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-flux-canalization, 2.2 cm:gasterosteus-aculeatus-branching-tree" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2007.10.055>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/376765a0>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/hdy.2011.1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1107239>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1182213> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-aculeatus-benthic-turing-wavelength-s0.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

